messages.content:
A tiny bakery website

Screens of this mockup, as a tree:
@home: the first screen of A tiny bakery website (this screen)
  @menu: Menu screen of a small bakery website listing breads, pastries and cakes with prices
    @sourdough-details: Details screen of Sourdough loaf at a small bakery, with price, ingredients and an add-to-order button
    @rye-details: Details screen of Rye seeded bread at a small bakery, with price, ingredients and an add-to-order button (not made yet)
    @croissant-details: Details screen of Butter croissant at a small bakery, with price, ingredients and an add-to-order button (not made yet)
    @cinnamon-roll-details: Details screen of Cinnamon roll at a small bakery, with price, ingredients and an add-to-order button (not made yet)
    @lemon-cake-details: Details screen of Lemon drizzle cake at a small bakery, with price, serving size and an order button (not made yet)
  @visit: Visit screen of a small bakery website with address, opening hours and a contact form
    @visit-thanks: Thank you screen after sending a message to a small bakery (not made yet)

The spec of this mockup: decisions every screen follows, one per line; a row with ? is not decided yet.
product.core-flow = @home → @menu → @visit
ui.nav = Home @home, Menu @menu, Visit @visit
ui.back = Back label at the top left of deeper pages
ui.colors = Warm brown brand color, clickable elements in brown with underline
data.bakery-info = Crumb & Crust Bakery, 14 Mill Lane, Open Mon-Sat 7:00-18:00, hello@crumbandcrust.example

Tabs of ui.nav: last on every screen, in this markup, one link per tab with the label and @name ui.nav gives it, exactly; the app marks the current tab: <nav data-ui="tabs"><a data-action="@name">Label</a>…</nav>. A ui.nav line names each tab by its label and @name.
Back of ui.back: where ui.back says, with its label, in this markup: <a data-ui="back" data-action="back">Label</a>. The tab screens have no Back. A ui.back line starts with the label Back shows, then where it sits.

Design it for a phone screen, 390 px wide.

This screen is a step of the main path (product.core-flow): one control on it must open @menu.

The screen as it is now:
<title>Bakery home</title>
<meta name="idea" content="Hero card with a featured bake and a single big call to action">
<article>
<h1>Crumb &amp; Co.</h1>
<p><small>Fresh bread and pastries, baked every morning</small></p>
<img alt="" style="width:100%;border-radius:12px;background:#e8c9a0;aspect-ratio:4/3;display:block">
<h2>Today's bake: Cardamom buns</h2>
<p>Warm, soft and dusted with pearl sugar. <mark>Only 24 left</mark></p>
<button data-action="@menu: Menu screen of a small bakery website listing breads, pastries and cakes with prices">See the full menu</button>
</article>
<fieldset>
<legend>This week</legend>
<p><strong>Sourdough loaf</strong> · 6.50</p>
<p><strong>Almond croissant</strong> · 3.20</p>
<p><strong>Lemon tart</strong> · 4.00</p>
</fieldset>
<progress value="24" max="40" aria-label="Buns baked today"></progress>
<p><small id="count">24 of 40 buns baked today</small></p>
<nav data-ui="tabs">
<a data-action="@home" aria-current="page">Home</a>
<a data-action="@menu: Menu screen of a small bakery website listing breads, pastries and cakes with prices">Menu</a>
<a data-action="@visit: Visit screen of a small bakery website with address, opening hours and a contact form">Visit</a>
</nav>
<script>
(function(){
var n=24;
var c=document.getElementById('count');
var p=document.querySelector('progress');
c.textContent=n+' of 40 buns baked today';
p.value=n;
})();
</script>

Reply with this screen again with one change; keep everything else as it is, including its data-action links, and add no second control for a screen it already links to. If the change is a rule other screens should follow too (how something looks or works, or what a value means), add a <meta name="spec" content="key = value"> line for it after the idea, e.g. <meta name="spec" content="ui.seat-map = Seats as a grid, taken seats grey">. The change: Make the main heading say "Fresh bread daily"

